Projects the relay into every verified installed AI client's MCP
config: each stdio server bound to an approved vserver is REPLACED by
the stdio relay (`observer mcp-relay wrap --client <tool> --server
<key>`), and the approved vservers are added as remote entries through
the relay's loopback listener when one is configured and remote
forwarding is wired. Every original is journaled with a verbatim
backup BEFORE it is rewritten; `observer mcp unwrap` puts it back.
An entry with no approved binding is NOT wrapped and is reported.

Refuses (writing nothing) when [mcp_relay].enabled = false.

The relay rides the daemon's :8820. Never stop/restart the daemon while an
MCP session or a proxied route is live: route OFF -> stop -> relaunch ->
route ON, as one atomic op (docs/daemon-restart-runbook.md).

Usage:
  observer mcp wrap [flags]

Flags:
      --config string   path to config.toml (default ~/.observer/config.toml)
  -h, --help            help for wrap
      --no-remote       do not resolve remote forwarding (no org-server registration call; remote entries are not projected)
